# ntdll/tests: Don't run reparse point checks after NtCreateFile fails.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11760 state=closed
# Under Wine, the NtCreateFile() call that opens testreparse_dirlink in
test_reparse_points() fails with STATUS_IO_REPARSE_DATA_INVALID and
leaves the handle NULL. The checks that follow keep using the bad
handle, so NtQueryDirectoryFile() returns without filling the output
buffer. The test then reads the uninitialized buffer as a
FILE_DIRECTORY_INFORMATION chain, uses NextEntryOffset as a byte offset,
and dereferences the result. This terminates the process and prevents the
remainder of the test suite from running.

Guard all the checks that depend on the bad handle up to where it is
opened again. The failure is still reported, and later checks that open
their own handle are unaffected.
